  "numerical_characteristics": {
    "dtype": "float32",
    "precision": null,
    "magnitude": "around a scale of 100_000 for a feature",
    "tolerance": null,
    "category_specific_evidence": [
      "RidgeGCV is not very numerically stable with float32: it casts the input to float64 unless the device and namespace combination does not allow float64 (specifically torch with mps).",
      "Things start breaking down around a scale of 100_000 for a feature.",
      "In test_ridge_array_api_compliance, there was conditional logic for RidgeGCV with float32 that set tols['rtol'] = 1e-3 when _max_precision_float_dtype(...) == xp.float32.",
      "The conditional tolerance behavior was removed from the test: it now calls check(...) without any tols overrides."
    ],
    "reproduction_risks": [
      "If the repro targets float32 behavior for RidgeGCV, it must consider whether float64 is allowed by the array API namespace/device; torch with mps is called out as a case where float64 is not allowed.",
      "If the repro targets the reported breakdown, it must include a feature magnitude regime around 100_000, since that scale is explicitly where things start breaking down.",
      "If comparing correct vs incorrect answers, the evidence only specifies an rtol separation of 1e-3 in one prior test branch (RidgeGCV+float32); the current test no longer sets this tolerance, so the repro must align with the code/version behavior being tested."
    ]
  },
